      <title>I wrote Distromatch, shall we use it?</title>
      <subtitle></subtitle>
      <track>CrossDistribution Devroom</track>
      <type></type>
      <language></language>
      <abstract>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;At the &lt;a href=&#34;http://distributions.freedesktop.org/wiki/Meetings/AppInstaller2011&#34;&gt;AppInstaller2011&lt;/a&gt; meeting I started writing &lt;a href=&#34;http://www.enricozini.org/2011/debian/distromatch/&#34;&gt;Distromatch&lt;/a&gt; which is able to map binary package names across different distribution using a wide set of euristics.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Distromatch has the potential of being a radical change in cross-distro cooperation, enabling exchange of package screenshots, categories, ratings, reviews and many other interesting kinds of metadata.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Since distromatch has existed for almost a year and (afaik) so far none of this has happened, I am taking advantage of the cross-distro room to show how it works and discuss how to move on from here.&lt;/p&gt;      </abstract>
